  "id": "huaylas_mantaro",
  "name": "Huaylas (Mantaro Valley carnival dance-song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Huaylas, or huaylarsh, is the carnival courtship dance of the Mantaro Valley around Huancayo in Junín, rooted in the valley's agrarian festivities and now played in two broad styles: the older huaylas antiguo and the faster, competition-driven huaylas moderno. Its modern sound is the Junín orquesta típica of saxophones, clarinets, violins and Andean harp, often with a sung verse before the instrumental sections.",
  "recipe": "classic modern huaylas, carnival Processional, andean branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment. yellow brass modern standard saxophone, grenadilla African blackwood traditional clarinet, fiddle, arpa peruana. mountain valley. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
